cuju reimplements Google Research Football (https://github.com/google-research/football),
Copyright 2019 Google LLC, Apache License 2.0. Its engine descends from Gameplay Football by
Bastiaan Konings Schuiling, dedicated to the public domain. Files that carry a Google line, apart
from those of python/cuju/gfootball, were rewritten from that code by the cuju Authors in 2026.
animations.bin and the asset bundles are derived from the data and scenarios of Google Research
Football.
cuju is not affiliated with or endorsed by Google.

include/cuju/libm ports math functions of the GNU C Library 2.39 (LGPL 2.1 or later). Where Arm
Optimized Routines v21.02 (MIT, Copyright Arm Limited) or FreeBSD's msun (the notice of Sun
Microsystems, Inc.) holds the same code, the port is taken from there under that license. Each file
reproduces its upstream notices and names its license. The libraries of cuju compile these
functions in, and the complete source of each release is published with it.

python/cuju/gfootball holds the Python package of Google Research Football 2.10.3, commit 3d9e754,
Copyright 2019 Google LLC, Apache License 2.0, with its import lines changed by the cuju Authors.
ci/make/port_gfootball.py lists each change, and every Python file keeps Google's header.

python/cuju/gfootball/_gym/_vendored holds the core of gym 0.21.0, Copyright 2016 OpenAI, MIT
License, with its import lines and its plugin loader changed by the cuju Authors.
LICENSES/MIT-gym.txt holds its license.

packages/cuju-gfootball holds the package cuju-gfootball, the cuju Authors' own code under the
Apache License 2.0, which maps GRF's module names onto python/cuju/gfootball and holds none of GRF's
files. Its wheel carries a copy of LICENSE.

The world RNG follows Boost.Random (Boost Software License 1.0). The episode seeds follow MT19937
by Makoto Matsumoto and Takuji Nishimura (BSD-3-Clause), as CPython's random module uses it.

src/render, cuju's software renderer, reproduces the frames that GRF draws on Mesa 25.2.8's
llvmpipe driver. It ports algorithms of Mesa's llvmpipe, gallivm, draw and u_blitter code
(https://mesa3d.org, MIT License, Copyright VMware, Inc. and other Mesa authors), and its programs
follow GRF's shaders (Apache License 2.0) as llvmpipe compiles them. LICENSES/MIT-Mesa.txt holds
Mesa's license. src/render/pixels.cpp ports RGB to gray conversion and area resizing from OpenCV 5.0
(https://opencv.org, Apache License 2.0, the OpenCV authors). src/render/overlay2d ports the alpha
blit of SDL 2.30.0, Copyright 1997-2024 Sam Lantinga, the smoothed zoom of SDL2_gfx 1.0.4, Copyright
2012-2014 Andreas Schiffler, and the text layout of SDL_ttf 2.22.0, Copyright 2001-2024 Sam
Lantinga, all under the zlib License, which LICENSES/Zlib.txt holds. The cuju Authors wrote these
ports in 2026, and each ported file names its source and is marked as altered.

packaging/cuju-grf-media builds the data package cuju-grf-media, which ci/make/make_render_media.py
fills with media of Google Research Football copied unchanged, for cuju's software renderer. Its
models, textures and images descend from Gameplay Football and are dedicated to the public domain
under the Unlicense, Google's changes are licensed under the Apache License 2.0, and its font,
Alegreya Sans SC, Copyright 2013 The Alegreya Sans Project Authors, is licensed under the SIL Open
Font License 1.1. LICENSES/Unlicense.txt and LICENSES/OFL-1.1.txt hold the two licenses, and
packaging/cuju-grf-media/NOTICE gives the details, among them a note on the trademarks that its
adboard images show. No wheel of cuju holds these files.

